        <figure>
            <img src="img/networking.jpg" alt="A visual of one computer using routing and forwarding to communicate with a second computer.">
        </figure>
        <p class="networking-entry-text">
            Networking is largely about the interconnection of various machines either across different networks using routers, or within local networks using switches.
            Routers use "routing" to determine the path a packet takes across a network, while forwarding is the process in which a router
            actually sends the packet to the next hop or stepping stone within the path that has been chosen.
            Depending on which protocol is being used a router may be given the topology of its routing area, or it may learn about reachable networks from its neighbors.

        </p>
